ks.jks
app-signed.apk
app-unsigned.apk
app-aligned.apk
build/
classes.dex
*.tmp
# Signing material must never be committed or shipped: supply it via KS/KS_PASS.
# A signing key is the one file whose leak is not repairable by reissuing: an APK
# signed with a different key cannot update an installed com.macchanger at all,
# so the user must uninstall and lose the app-private NVRAM backup.
ks.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pk8
*.pem
*.der
*.key
# The audit (AUDIT.md, audit/) quotes the removed keystore password and the
# vulnerable code, and is not written for users.  tools/package.sh already
# excludes it from the archive it builds; this keeps 'git add -A' + commit from
# putting it into a history that a clone or a hand-off would then carry.  The
# files stay in the working tree: they are the record of why this tree changed.
AUDIT.md
audit/

